# Crawlora {{display_name}} Go client

Focused Go module for the Crawlora {{display_name}} API, generated from its selected public OpenAPI contract.
Current module version: `{{version}}`.

```sh
go get {{module_path}}@latest
```

```go
package main

import (
	"context"
	"fmt"

	"{{module_path}}"
)

func main() {
	client := {{package_name}}.NewClient("your-crawlora-api-key")
	defer client.Close()
	result, err := client.Call(context.Background(), "{{sample_operation}}", {{package_name}}.{{sample_params}})
	if err != nil {
		panic(err)
	}
	fmt.Println(result)
}
```

The client exposes `{{operation_count}}` {{display_name}} operation IDs through `OperationIDs` and direct methods for the selected operations. `Call` accepts a `Params` map and enforces this module's operation allowlist. Set `BaseURL`, `Timeout`, or `HTTPClient` on `Client` to customize requests. Text transcript/feed responses are returned as strings; JSON responses are decoded into Go values.

API keys can be passed to `NewClient` or supplied with `CRAWLORA_API_KEY`. The only default request destination is Crawlora's hosted API at `https://api.crawlora.net/api/v1`.

Create an account at [crawlora.net](https://crawlora.net/signup), then open the [Crawlora console](https://crawlora.net/app) to get an API key. See the [API documentation](https://crawlora.net/docs) or visit [the general Go SDK](https://github.com/Crawlora-org/crawlora-go-sdk) for shared API-key setup.
